# .muse — thinking kernel (Xerox Utility)
Thinker: MUSE. 1 Thinking + 1 Launch session. No THINKING.md (not requested).

## Core value
Never miss a scan; save where I want with name/format I want; zero hunting in scan.htm.

## Decisions
| D | Why |
|---|---|
| Sidecar, not clone | Keep Scan3/TWAIN; only watch/notify/save = smaller, safer |
| Watch ALL boxes | Notification must show which folder used; auto-discover, no hardcode |
| Watermark per-box (fileNo+date+filename TS) | Ignore 17 old files on first run; catch up after PC-off/network-drop |
| Lazy download | List/metadata on poll; full TIFF only on expand/click = light |
| Post-transfer popup `Delete from device?` + bulk delete in GUI | Prevent pile-up/re-notify; delete only on confirm |
| Sidebar + cards (small→expanded preview) + Settings (IP+checker, default store folder) | Modern UX; fallback folder if user picks none |
| Python modern UI | User choice; fastest HTTP/convert/toast path |

## OUT
No folder/user creation on device, no print, no SNMP/SOAP/TWAIN parity.

## Risks / unknowns
- Retrieve + delete `.cmd` shape open (need read-only tail probe of Retrieve form).
- Password boxes: need per-box auth test; Box1 open, others unknown.
- Multi-PC race: if A deletes, B misses; accept v1, note it.
- TIFF multipage fidelity; toast persistence limits on Win.

## For executor
Prove download+delete read-first, then poller→notify→cards→save/convert→settings. Success = better UI/UX now, automation-ready next.
